Entrepreneurs look at the value chain of a product or a service to
pinpoint where the value chain can be made more effective or to spot where
additional “value” can be added in some meaningful way. This type of analy-
sis may focus on (1) a single primary activity of the value chain (such as
marketing and sales), (2) the interface between one stage of the value chain
and another (such as the interface between operations, which are the activi-
